  "chapter": 491,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 15 Chapter 491\n\n       MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 7756, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT to amend the education law, in relation to required attend-\n        ances\"\n\n    APPROVED\n\n  This legislation would  direct  school  boards  to  determine  whether\nschool  sessions  should  be held on a day where a religious or cultural\nholiday would lead to a waste of educational resources  due  to  signif-\nicant   absenteeism.  A  district  may  make  this  determination  on  a\ndistrict-wide or individual school basis. This  bill  will  ensure  that\ndistricts consider the impact of the school calendar on students' abili-\nty to observe religious and cultural holidays.\n\n  However,  it  is important to note that this bill has no effect on the\nrequirement that school districts provide 180 days of instruction or the\nState aid implications if a school fails to meet  this  requirement.  In\naddition,  this  legislation  does  not  excuse  a  school district from\ncomplying with its  obligation  to  conduct  State  assessments  on  the\ndate(s)  scheduled  by  the State Education Department. With this under-\nstanding, I am signing this bill.\n\n  The bill is approved.                       (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2014
 },
